course: dictionary
lesson: 13685
title: A firm order
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An injunction is an order. It tells someone that they must do something, or must not do something. Often a judge in a court gives it. «The judge gave him an injunction: he must not go near her house.» So the word tells you an official order has been given.
explain: You will hear this word in the news and in grown-up talk. «The court granted an injunction to stop the company cutting down the trees.» Granted means the court agreed to it and made the order. Look for clue words like court, judge, must and must not.
explain: The word can also mean a very firm instruction, even when no court is involved. «His mother's injunction was to be home before dark.» Nobody went to court there. It was a strong, serious order from his mum. Ask yourself: is there a court or judge nearby? If yes, it is the law meaning. If not, it means a firm instruction.
fact: An injunction is an order that someone must do something, or must not do something.
fact: In law, a court or judge usually gives an injunction.
fact: «Injunction» can also mean a firm warning or instruction, as in «his mother's injunction to be home before dark».
fact: Injunction is a noun: one injunction, two injunctions.
fact: Clue words that often appear near injunction are court, judge, order, must and must not.
exercise: «The judge gave him an injunction: he must not go near her house.» What does injunction mean here? | A fancy word for a long walk | A new house for the family | A happy prize for good behaviour | *An order from a court telling him what he must not do
exercise: «His mother's injunction was to be home before dark.» What does injunction mean here? | A question about the time | *A firm instruction he is expected to follow | A painting of the night sky | A picnic in the park
exercise: Which word in «The court granted an injunction to stop the noise» tells you this is an official order? | the | *court | stop | noise
test: «She got an injunction to stop him coming near the house.» What does injunction mean? | A loud noise | A friend who lives nearby | A type of cake | *An official order not to do something
test: Ella says an injunction is a happy surprise. Is she right? | No, it is a small fish | Yes, it is a holiday | Yes, it is a happy surprise | *No, it is an order that someone must or must not do something
exam: Look at «The judge's injunction stopped the company from cutting down the trees.» What does injunction mean? | A picture of the trees in the park | A plan to plant more trees | *A legal order that the company must not do something | A gift from the company to the town
